{
  "note": "Shared corpus: the browser verdict (js/engine.js, the field the user sees) and the server verdict (CheckCharacter::validateSingleField / validatePooledField as UniversalValidator::findingsCheck calls them) for the same value. browser is \"blank\" (no message), \"valid\" or \"invalid\". server is \"skip\" (findingsCheck skips the value as blank), \"valid\", \"not-checked\" (the server cannot tell what the browser RegExp makes of the value and reports it for a manual check) or the reason of the finding. Locks VAL-1 (no fail-open on characters outside printable ASCII), VAL-3 (both sides trim the same whitespace) and VAL-12 (the 512-unit cap). Expectations were written from the definitions and checked against both runtimes; a row that changes is a parity change, not a fixture refresh.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "why": "the default rule (mod 37,36 hybrid, default strip, no pattern): whitespace the browser trims is not part of the ID; any other character outside printable ASCII makes the check fail on both sides",
      "rule": { "type": "single" },
      "rows": [
        ["FC1-0589C", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589D", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\n", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589C\r\n", "valid", "valid"],
        ["\tFC1-0589C", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589C\f", "valid", "valid"],
        [" ", "blank", "skip"],
        ["\n", "blank", "skip"],
        ["\t", "blank", "skip"],
        ["FC1-0589C\u00A0", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589D\u00A0", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["\uFEFFFC1-0589D", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\u3000", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589\u0421", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\u200B", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-\uFF10589C", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["garbage\nvalue", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\nFC1-0589D", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1\t0589D", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589D\u007F", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\uD83D\uDE00", "invalid", "check-character"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "the same with strip \"-\": the delimiter set does not change how the edges are trimmed",
      "rule": {
        "type": "single",
        "strip": "-"
      },
      "rows": [
        ["FC1-0589C", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589D", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\n", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589C\r\n", "valid", "valid"],
        ["\tFC1-0589C", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589C\f", "valid", "valid"],
        [" ", "blank", "skip"],
        ["\n", "blank", "skip"],
        ["\t", "blank", "skip"],
        ["FC1-0589C\u00A0", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589D\u00A0", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["\uFEFFFC1-0589D", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\u3000", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589\u0421", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\u200B", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-\uFF10589C", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["garbage\nvalue", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\nFC1-0589D", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1\t0589D", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589D\u007F", "invalid", "check-character"],
        ["FC1-0589C\uD83D\uDE00", "invalid", "check-character"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "why": "a format-only rule: the pattern decides alone, and a character outside printable ASCII that the pattern cannot match is a format miss on both sides",
      "rule": {
        "type": "single",
        "algorithm": "none",
        "idPattern": "FC[0-9]-[0-9]{4}[0-9A-Z]"
      },
      "rows": [
        ["FC1-0589C", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589D", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589C\n", "valid", "valid"],
        ["FC1-0589C\r\n", "valid", "valid"],
